<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Champotón</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1537 CE (approx.) · capital Champotón</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maya province on the Campeche coast whose warriors killed the first Spanish expedition's leader in 1517, later Montejo's base for conquering Yucatán.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Champotón, the Chakanputun of the Maya chronicles, was an ancient coastal town associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itza-people">Itza</a> before their rise at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chichen-itza">Chichen Itza</a>. After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441 it emerged as an independent province on the western coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán</a> peninsula.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The province was ruled by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kowoj">Couoh</a> lineage from the town of Champotón at the mouth of a river, which lived from fishing, salt and coastal trade. In 1517 its lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moch-couoh">Moch Couoh</a> led warriors who defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-hernandez-de-cordoba-founder-of-nicaragua">Francisco Hernández de Córdoba's</a> expedition, mortally wounding him. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-grijalva">Grijalva</a>'s expedition fought there again in 1518.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1537 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo-the-younger">Francisco de Montejo the Younger</a> established a Spanish base at Champotón, from which the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán</a> was launched. The province was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>, and the town survives in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a> state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1441 CE – 1537 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.38%;width:1.91%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1537 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Champotón</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Moch Couoh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chakanputun, Chanputun</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1489&amp;focus=champoton" aria-label="Champotón on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2228 1460 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Champotón lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2548 1716L2591 1670M2548 1716L4910 989M2548 1716L2590 1658"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2591 1670h0M4910 989h0M2590 1658h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2548 1716h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2548 1716h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Champotón. <a href="/atlas?year=1489&amp;focus=champoton">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
